WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.000
A payment webhook sends a receipt.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.100
The receipt is saved. The response is lost.

3
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.300
So the handler retries. One receipt, or two?

4
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:11.900
Your real handler. A modeled receipt service.

5
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:15.000
You choose the failure. You write the check.

6
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:21.300
The bug: each retry gets a new idempotency key.

7
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:25.100
The check fails. Two receipts were saved.

8
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:31.400
The fix: reuse the invoice ID as the key.

9
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.400
Same failure, same check. One receipt.

10
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.600
PASS means your checks held in this modeled run.

11
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:44.000
